if you're excited about GTA heists as  much as the rest of us you're going to  want to make sure you're ready that  means getting to the required level of  12 as soon as possible so I put together  a short list do's and don'ts to make  sure you level up quickly as a patch 2.0  for 360 and ps3 or patch 1.06 for Xbox  one and ps4 now these aren't cheats or  tricks that are just going to be patched  in a week this is a regular overview of  things you should just know when you're  looking to get levels join a crew  immediately there are tons of benefits  to being in a crew with lots of people  and the most important one is that you  get RP for playing with friends and crew  members you get a 20% bonus just for  completing a mission with a crew member  plus you get another 10% RP bonus if  they're your friend so get your friends  all on the same crew and complete  missions to increase your rank join  servers that have at least six people in  them you don't want to be anywhere alone  the more people in your server the  higher chance you'll have to run into  player bounties armored cars loot drops  and other free mode events you also get  small pockets of RP for doing things  with other people like riding in a car  and flying it's not a lot but it's  pretty much free RP so I can't stress it  enough join a crew if you don't know any  crews you can join GameSpot's crew we  have a stupid t-shirt you can wear but  more importantly we'll help you level up  use your newly acquired crew members and  friends and play contact missions use  quick jobs on your phone host and make  sure to click auto invite that'll invite  anyone currently in your crew to play  with you and it will help fill your game  up be patient and wait for about four  people to players on the same crew next  you 10% more cash three players gets you  20% and four players tops it out at 30%  that cash is going to come in handy in  your early levels so that you can buy  guns and cars so don't neglect it money  is valuable to put the difficulty up too  hard it'll earn you a 50% RP bonus plus  a cash bonus for anyone else in the  mission finally you can change the  targeting mode to free aim which will  give you an extra 25 % RP bonus for all  participants but be warned it makes it  pretty hard when the mission is over  don't forget to vote you get 50 RP for  each vote not much but over time that  [ __ ] adds up when your mission is over  try picking more missions they typically  have a larger payout they're the ones  with the stars  be on the lookout for higher ranked  contact mission invites this is again  where your crew and your friends come in  a low-level player can't play the higher  ranked missions by themselves if your  friend invites you it's all good and you  get that high RP that comes with it for  instance contact missions from Giraud  will not only typically result in more  RP and cash rewards but they're more  diverse and generally more fun take your  time in the missions most people want to  rush through and hurry to get the reward  but there's a duration multiplier that  gives you more payout for the longer  you're in the missions so you're getting  more money for each minute you're  actively trying to complete the  objective it maxes out after 16 minutes  but most missions don't take that long  so it's not really a problem you get RP  bonuses for headshots plus NPCs are down  for good you also get Awards with RP for  the first deaths with any particular  weapon so try out lots of different  weapons and always purchase the gear you  should avoid the open world and the  grind at first there are some highest  level players in that open world and  they will SWAT you like a casual fly so  stick to the missions if you're just  hanging out in the open world you could  rob a store it gives you about 150 RP  and a thousand bucks and for every  wanted star you lose you gain 100 RP if  you can get there you get 50 RP for each  minute you last with 5 stars but it's  not really as lucrative as it sounds if  you're looking at RP per minute it's  still best to do missions don't be  tricked into the car import requests  they take a long time and if your car  gets banged up you pay for it it comes  out of your pocket it can take 10  minutes to gain an easily 300 RP that's  only 30 RP a minute if you're in the  open world you could consider impromptu  short races that'll give you about 300  RP just for winning it only takes 30  seconds but you'll always find that the  best meet is in the missions with  higher-level friends and crew members so  watch for the invites and check the  levels of the missions landing strip got  me over 3,100 RP and over 18,000 in just  over 10 minutes  stick up the stick-up crew got me over  3200 RP and 17,000 cash in under 8  minutes and as you level up you'll  unlock your own missions that are pretty  good messed up only requires a level  seven so be on the lookout for that one  in five minutes you can get about 1,500  RP and over $8,000 cash you should pay  attention to the RP per minute but don't  get bogged down on time it's also  important to stop and remember that  you're playing a ridiculously beautiful  game in an incredibly immersive world  there's more than enough here to keep  you entertained for a long time so make  some friends and gain some levels while  having fun there's a lot more to get  into here but this is a good start we'll  probably be making another video for  quickly leveling once you get to 50 so  keep going and if you have any quick  tips and tricks put them in the comments  below see you in Los Santos simple it  should be the easiest money you'll ever  make  you
 

